    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate looking to capitalize on high-upside matchups, led by **Christian Yelich**, who paces our lineup with a 75.84 efficiency score. **Christian Yelich** draws a prime assignment against Feltner, where a combination of a +19% SP skill advantage and a +13% platoon edge makes him our most bankable asset. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (69.49) remains an elite start at 3B; despite a park penalty, his elite 0.376 xwOBA and favorable SP matchup against Bibee ensure he remains a cornerstone of our offensive production. **Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) also benefit from exploitable SP matchups, with **Casey Schmitt** receiving a notable late boost due to wind conditions blowing out, enhancing his power potential against Johnson.\n\nOur toughest roster decision centered on our bench, where **Josh Smith** (45.38) just narrowly missed the final utility spot. While **Josh Smith** carries a strong +14% platoon advantage against Woo, he ultimately couldn't surpass the efficiency of **Carson Benge** (46.38) or the sheer power profile of **Yordan Alvarez** (63.49). **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start regardless of the SP matchup, as his 0.478 xwOBA is simply too dangerous to keep on the pine. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the risk profiles of **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; both face elite arms in Weathers and Skenes, respectively. While their projected scores are solid, the -13% and -19% SP skill penalties reflect the high-strikeout nature of their matchups, necessitating a focus on their speed-based contributions to keep our SB category afloat. We are keeping **Caleb Durbin**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Hyeseong Kim** in reserve as we navigate the remaining game caps for the month.",
